{
  "changelog": "Initial release of geoskill-semantic-segmentation.\n\n- Implements per-pixel semantic segmentation for multispectral remote sensing imagery using offline numpy-based methods.\n- Supports both unsupervised (KMeans) and supervised (RandomForest) classification; supervised mode requires label rasters.\n- Performs sliding-window tiled prediction with stitching and majority-filter post-processing.\n- Includes synthetic data generation for testing and QA, along with real-image support.\n- Outputs GeoTIFF class raster, class statistics JSON, and a run manifest.\n- All processing is local and offline; no user data is uploaded.\n- MIT licensed.",
